atus\\\":\\\"active\\\",\\\"question\\\":\\\"Can a small prepared root sample show a measurable mass change against an untreated reference?\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"Root meals at ticks 3 and 40 each provided 14 realized nutrition; known root toxicity is 0.\\\",\\\"The tick-12 press trial consumed 0.1 root and recorded flexibility 0 at load 0.25.\\\",\\\"Heating failed because no heat source was in reach.\\\",\\\"Both compare-material-samples and beam-mass-comparator have been learned through study.\\\",\\\"At tick 44 I carry 5.9 roots, two branches and three stone units; Sol has an observed untested comparator nearby.\\\"],\\\"uncertainty\\\":\\\"My materials' suitability and instrument repeatability remain untested. No drying response or preservation benefit has been demonstrated.\\\",\\\"goal\\\":\\\"Maintain food reserves while developing a usable comparative measurement method.\\\",\\\"completedSteps\\\":[\\\"Gathered and ate roots.\\\",\\\"Observed a root plant and performed a small press trial.\\\",\\\"Learned sample preparation and beam comparator operation.\\\"],\\\"outputs\\\":[\\\"Known root nutrition and a recorded low-load press response.\\\",\\\"Learned measurement contracts, not validated equipment or drying results.\\\"],\\\"missing\\\":\\\"Suitable preparation edge and support, my own usable tested comparator, and actual before/after readings.\\\",\\\"next\\\":\\\"Observe carried stone, assess comparator requirements, and coordinate findings with Sol.\\\",\\\"pauseReason\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"benefit\\\":\\\"Existing food knowledge supports meals; assessment can identify missing requirements before committing materials.\\\"}],\\\"cares\\\":null,\\\"views\\\":{}}\"}","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"final_answer"}}

